      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/adal"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          aðal
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "[O. H. G. adal, <i>genus;</i> cp. also A. S. éðele, <i>nobilis;</i> Old Engl. and Scot. <i>ethel;</i> Germ. <i>edel;</i> eðla- and eðal- came from mod. Dan. into Icel. aðall, <i>nobility.</i> It does not occur in old writings in this sense.]",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/adal-vellir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          aðal-vellir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. pl. = óðalvellir, Rm.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/adild"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          aðild
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "older form <strong>aðilð,</strong> pl. ir, f. [root <strong>aðal</strong>], v. the following word aðili. It doubtless originally meant <i>chiefdom, headship,</i> but it only occurs in the limited legal sense of <i>chief-prosecutorship</i> or <i>defendantship,</i> and this only, as it seems, in Icel. not in Norse law. It is a standing word in the Icel. codes and histories of the Commonwealth. It became obsolete after the year 1272, and does not occur in the codes Jb. or Js. In early times there were no public prosecutions or lawsuits; the aðild devolved together with the erfð (<i>heirship</i>) on the principal male heir, if of age; erfð and aðild go together, the first as a right, the last as an incumbent duty, like an English trusteeship; til erfðar ok aðiðar, Eb. ch. 38. In the year 993 a law was passed to the effect that male heirs under sixteen years of age should be exempted from aðild, neither should heiresses ever be aðili. In such cases the aðild devolved on the next male heir above sixteen years of age, who then got a fee for executing this duty, Bs. i. 675. The aðild also could be undertaken by a delegate, called at fara með handselda sök, sök handseld, vörn handseld, fara með sök, <i>carry on a suit</i>, etc., v. Grágás Vs. ch. 35, (of aðild in a case of manslaughter,) and in many other places ; Eb. ch. 38, Bs. i. 675 (Rs. in fine), Bjarn. (in fine), Njála, and many others: v. Dasent, Introd. to Burnt Njal.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/adildar-madr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          aðilðar-maðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. = aðili, Sturl. iii. 240, Orkn. 212.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/adili"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          aðili
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "ja, m. <i>the chief-defendant</i> or <i>prosecutor</i> in an Icel. lawsuit in the time of the Commonwealth. It seems to have meant originally <i>head, chieftain, princeps</i>. A standing word in the Grágás and the Sagas. As to the form, the older one is that which preserves the <i>j</i> in the terminations, gen. dat. acc. aðilja, plur. -jar, acc. -ja, dat. -jum. The Grágás constantly employs this form. The Njála and some of the Sagas drop the <i>j</i> and write aðila etc. In the Grágás aðilja seems to occur as an indecl. word—at least four times in the Kb.—used as nom. pl.: but as -ar in old MSS. is frequently marked by a single ‘a’ with a little stroke (a-), this may be a misinterpretation. The indeclinable form occurs in the Kb. (Þ. Þ.) 25 and 109 (only preserved in the Kb.); Kb. 147, 170 has aðilja, where the Sb. has in both passages aðiljar: cp. however guðsifja and -bræðra. There is a distinction between a sóknar-aðili or sakar-aðili, <i>prosecutor</i>, and a varnar-aðili, <i>defendant</i>. Either with gen. or prep. <i>at</i>, varnar-a., sóknar-a., sakar-a.; or inversely, a. sakar, a. varnar, a. frumsakar, Kb. 42, 124; a. máls, 126; a. vígsakar, in a case of manslaughter, 167; or vígsakar a. (often); a. fésakar, in a lawsuit about compensation, 123; a. legorðssakar, case of legorð, 194: with <i>at</i>, varnir þær er hann er aðili at, 175; aðili at legorðs sekt, App. iv. 46, Grág. Kb. 15, 211 ; cp. also § 58, p. 103: hann er aðili at sök, bæði sækjandi ok seljandi, <i>chief-plaintiff, either for carrying it on himself or by a delegate</i>, Kb. 208. In the case of a delegate being the aðili, the challenge of jurors and judges on account of relationship was to be made in respect to the chief aðili, not the delegate, Kb. 127.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/adils"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          aðils
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "[A. S. <i>Eâdgils</i>], a pr. name, the name of the mythical Swed. king at Upsala, Edda 82; also on the Runic stones in the Isle of Man.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "prep. often used elliptically by dropping the case, or even merely adverbially, [Ulf. <i>af</i>; A. S. and Engl. <i>of</i>, <i>off</i>; Hel. <i>ab</i>; Germ. <i>ab</i>; Gr. <i>άπό</i>; Lat. <i>a</i>, <i>ab</i>.] With dat. denoting a motion <i>a loco</i>; one of the three prepp. <i>af</i>, <i>ór</i>, <i>frá</i>, corresponding to those <i>in loco</i>—<i>á</i>, <i>í</i>, <i>við</i>, and <i>ad locum</i>—<i>á</i>, <i>í</i>, <i>at</i>. It in general corresponds to the prepp. <i>in loco</i>—<i>á</i>, or <i>in locum</i>—<i>til</i>, whilst <i>ór</i> answers more to <i>í</i>; but it also frequently corresponds to <i>yfir</i>, <i>um</i> or <i>í</i>. It ranges between <i>ór</i> and <i>frá</i>, generally denoting the idea <i>from the surface of</i>, while <i>ór</i> means <i>from the inner part</i>, and <i>frá from the outer part</i> or <i>border</i>. The motion from a <i>hill</i>, <i>plain</i>, <i>open place</i> is thus denoted by <i>af</i>; by <i>ór</i> that from an <i>enclosed space</i>, <i>depth</i>, <i>cavity</i>, thus <i>af</i> fjalli, but <i>ór</i> of a <i>valley</i>, <i>dale</i>; <i>af</i> Englandi, but <i>ór</i> Danmörk, as <i>mörk</i> implies the notion of a <i>deep wood</i>, <i>forest</i>. The wind blows <i>af</i> landi, but a ship sets sail <i>frá</i> landi; <i>frá</i> landi also means a <i>distance from: af</i> hendi, of a <i>glove</i>, <i>ring</i>; <i>ór</i> hendi, of whatever has been <i>kept in the hand</i> (correl. to <i>á</i> hendi and <i>í</i> hendi). On the other hand <i>af</i> is more general, whilst <i>frá</i> and <i>ór</i> are of a more special character; <i>frá</i> denoting a <i>departure</i>, <i>ór</i> an <i>impulse</i> or <i>force</i>; a member goes home <i>af</i> þingi, whereas <i>ór</i> may denote an <i>inmate</i> of a district, or convey the notion of <i>secession</i> or <i>exclusion from</i>, Eb. 105 new Ed.; the traveller goes <i>af</i> landi, the exile <i>ór</i> landi: taka e-t <i>af</i> e-m is to take a thing <i>out of one’s hand</i>, that of taka <i>frá</i> e-m <i>to remove</i> out of one’s sight, etc. In general <i>af</i> answers to Engl. <i>of</i>, <i>off</i>, <i>ór</i> to <i>out of</i>, and <i>frá</i> to <i>from</i>: the Lat. prepp. <i>ab</i>, <i>de</i>, and <i>ex</i> do not exactly correspond to the Icelandic, yet as a rule <i>ór</i> may answer to <i>ex</i>, <i>af</i> sometimes to <i>ab</i>, sometimes to <i>de</i>. <i>Of, off, from among; with, by; on account of by means of, because of concerning, in respect of</i>.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-audit"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-auðit
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. pass.; verða a. e-s, <i>to fail, have bad luck,</i> Gísl. 61.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-at"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-át
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "= ofát, <i>over-eating, gluttony, gormandizing.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-blomgadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-blómgaðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. pass. <i>‘off-bloomed,’ deflowered,</i> 655 xxxii. 3.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-bod"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-boð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>threats, high words,</i> Fms. x. 199; ofboð, n., is used of <i>panic</i>, <i>fear, agony,</i> and as a prefix in compds of boðs = <i>exceedingly.</i> So now the modern verb ofbjóða, mostly used impers., e-m ofbýðr, <i>to be shocked at</i>, etc.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-bragd"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-bragð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. used of persons, <i>a superior, excellent person;</i> hann var a. í vizku sinni, <i>wonderfully clever,</i> Fms. x. 397; a. annarra manna, <i>man of mark,</i> vi. 144. 2. gen. afbragðs is now frequently used as a prefix to nouns to express something <i>surpassing</i>—a. fagr, góðr, fríðr, etc.—a. vænleikr, <i>surpassing beauty,</i> Stj. 195.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-brigd"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-brigð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "and rarely <strong>afbrigði,</strong> n.—the compound afbrigðar-tré points to a fem.—<i>deviation, transgression, offence,</i> (cp. bregða af, <i>to deviate from</i>) esp. in pl., þeir sökuðu hann um nokkuð afbrigð þinga sinna, Post. 645. 97; sættarof ok afbrigð við guð, <i>trespasses,</i> 671. i; afbrigð, <i>wrongs,</i> Ld. 66; í afbrigðum boðorða Guðs, <i>transgressions against the commandments of God,</i> 671. 3; Þórðr afsakar sik um öll afbrigði við þik, <i>for having wronged thee,</i> Sturl. ii. 132, Fms. vii. 24, Ísl. ii. 201.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-brot"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-brot
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl. <i>trespasses, sin,</i> K. Á. 36, Fms. xi. 443; very frequent in religious writings after the Reformation.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-brugdning"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-brugðning
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>deviation from,</i> 656 B. 7.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-brudigr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-brúðigr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "and <strong>ábrúðigr,</strong> adj. <i>jealous,</i> Str. 5, 75; v. the following.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-bryda"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-brýða
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "dd, [af- intens. and brúðr, <i>sponsa</i>], <i>to be jealous,</i> also contracted <strong>ábrýða</strong>; þeir vandlæta ok afbrýða sem karldýrin eru borin, Stj. 94.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-brydi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-brýði
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "and contr. <strong>ábrýði,</strong> f. (now obsol.) <i>jealousy;</i> en er Sisinnus sá Clemens páfa standa hjá konu sinni, þá, viltist hugr hans mjök af mikilli ílsku ok afbrýði, Clem. 41, 42, Fms. i. 9, Ýt. 11; in all these places spelt with af-, but ábryði is more common, and occurs Hkr. i. 111; in the poem Gkv. i. 10—hon ægði mér af ábrýði—it is used of the jealousy of a wife to her husband.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-burdr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-burðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. (also spelt abb-), <i>odds, balance, bias, success</i> (cp. bera af, <i>to prevail</i>); kvað honum eigi annat vænna til afburðar, <i>in order to get the better of it,</i> Sd. 166; sá hann at engi varð afburðrinn, <i>they fought ‘aequo Marte,’</i> Sturl. ii. 74; hann ætlaði sér afburð, <i>he meant to keep the odds in his own hand,</i> Ísl. ii. 450; skal nú faraí haustvíking, ok vilda ek, at hon yrði eigi með minnum afburðum, <i>less glorious,</i> Orkn. 464.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-bud"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-búð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>an ‘off-booth,’ side-booth, apartment,</i> Korm. 116.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-dalr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-dalr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>an ‘off-dale,’ remote valley;</i> freq. in tales and rhymes of <i>hidden valleys,</i> esp. in pl., e. g. Hvað hét hundr karls er í afdölum bjó, in a nursery rhyme, K. Þ. K. 38, Fms. v. 183.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-deilingr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-deilingr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>part, portion, share,</i> Bs. i. 881.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-drattr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-dráttr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [draga af, <i>to detract</i>], <i>diminution, deduction,</i> Ann. 1358 (of <i>duties, fines</i>), Dipl. i. 7, Jm. 135 <i>= costs.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-drep"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-drep
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>shelter,</i> in a storm, Skýr. 318.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-drif"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-drif
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl. [drifa], <i>destiny, fate;</i> barn líkligt til stórra afdrifa, <i>a bairn likely to grow into a great man,</i> Fms. iii. 112 (of an exposed child); þykir mér lítil okkur a. verða munu, <i>inglorious life,</i> Fær. 53. It is now also used of <i>final fate, end.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-drykkja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-drykkja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>over-drinking, drunkenness,</i> = ofdrykkja [af- intens.]",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-eggja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-eggja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to dissuade,</i> (as we might say <i>‘to egg off’</i>), Fms. ix. 352.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-eira"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-eira
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "ð, <i>to curtail, deprive of,</i> with dat. of the thing; a. þá sinni sæmd, <i>to disgrace them,</i> Bær. 3; riddaradómi, <i>to degrade</i> from knighthood, 4.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/af-eista"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
          ref={[Function]}
        >
          af-eista
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "t, <i>to castrate,</i> Bs. ii. 118.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
